      "writtenOn": "2023-08-07T19:38:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In your scheme, it\u0027s technically possible that two calls to getOrCreateStateMachine interleave their `get()` calls where one thinks the map is empty for the device, _starts_ to make a new one, then the other thinks the map is empty for the device because the first hasn\u0027t put its new state machine in yet. Then we end up with two state machines.\n\nIt looks overcomplicated, but the putIfAbsent call will atomically put an object in the map if the object is miss at that time, avoiding that race condition. I couldn\u0027t think of a better way to avoid that situation (besides fixing the calling code to just \"not do that\").",
      "parentUuid": "2d9da9e7_c6e157c0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 446,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 460,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "44b6fc7568e1b911b44b1f8b327efaa3a303cefb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7ea9b40a_e80338fc",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/a2dpsink/A2dpSinkService.java",
