        "id": 1985170
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-07T20:07:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Synchronizing the method should probably help.\nDuring the lifecycle of the BT stack, majority of get* calls will mostly return the existing state machine. So, it ends up creating the object and being discarded immediately. If the construction of a state machine is a heavy operation, then tt would end up as an unnecessary spike.",
      "parentUuid": "bd15356c_ed37c2e8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 446,
        "startChar": 0,
