      "writtenOn": "2023-08-07T19:38:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this function really should act like the other profiles\u0027 `getOrCreateStateMachine`, and probably shouldn\u0027t remove the existing device without discrimination if one already exists. As such, this isn\u0027t probably what I\u0027d suggest.\n\nThat said, FWIW, I think there\u0027s problems here too, like a similar race condition in A2DP and AVRCP, but the solution is a bit more structural in nature (i.e. creating a state machine in MAP also starts it, this function is super ugly and clearly has some hacks applied to it to solve one-off bugs instead of addressing structural things, etc.). The topic of another CL though I suppose!",
